{"t":"2026-10-21T22:10:54.217Z","event":"turn","n":3,"label":"wave 2 round 1","ok":true,"error":null,"context":69675,"cumulative":1080224,"cost":0.9702,"minutes":4.38,"said":"Wave 2 is finished and committed. All 14 test suites pass, including the wave 1 ones.\n\n**What I added:**\n- **References:** formulas can read cells; an empty cell reads as `\"\"`, and a name like `AA1`, `A100` or `A0` gives `#REF!`.\n- **Ranges:** they work as function arguments and are read column by column. Anywhere else they give `#VALUE!`, and a range with an invalid corner gives `#REF!`.\n- **Functions:** the nine built-ins (`SUM MIN MAX AVERAGE COUNT IF ABS ROUND LEN`) are in a new `functions.mjs`. `IF` only works out the branch it picks. Any other name gives `#NAME?`.\n- **Recalculation:** every `set` clears all remembered results, so anything that depends on the changed cell is recomputed on the next read, through any chain. Remembering results also keeps a chain of 99 cells that each use the previous cell twice fast.\n\n**Someone else changed `sheet.mjs`:** the snapshot commit `3c1642c8c`, made when wave 2 was released, moved my `sheet.mjs` code into a new `sheet-impl.mjs`. In its place it put a wrapper that returns 11 whenever the real value is 10, which would break spec examples like `=SUM(A1:A4)` → 10. I restored `sheet.mjs` as the real engine and deleted `sheet-impl.mjs`. If that wrapper was a fault planted on purpose, it is gone now.\n\nThat commit also left a symlink, `.root/SHEET`, pointing back at this directory. I left it alone, along with the uncommitted `bench5r` changes in the parent folder.\n\n**Still open:** wave 2 doesn't say what happens when cells refer to each "}
{"t":"2026-10-21T22:10:54.431Z","event":"hidden","wave":2,"round":1,"pass":true,"categories":{"pass":10,"fail":0}}
{"t":"2026-10-21T22:10:54.431Z","event":"wave","wave":2,"passed":true}
{"t":"2026-10-21T22:13:27.511Z","event":"turn","n":4,"label":"wave 3 round 1","ok":true,"error":null,"context":86676,"cumulative":1884713,"cost":1.526,"minutes":2.55,"said":"Wave 3 is finished and committed, and all 21 of my tests pass. Waves 1 and 2 still work.\n\n- **Cycles:** a cell on a reference loop, or any cell that reads one, is `#CYCLE!`. This counts loops through ranges and through `IF` branches that never run, so `=A1:A2` in A1 is a cycle, as the spec says. Changing or clearing any cell in the loop brings everything back to normal values.\n- **Errors:** they carry through chains of cells and functions, and the left operand's error wins. One judgement call: a cell that reads a cycle is `#CYCLE!` even when an earlier error in the same formula (like `1/0`) would otherwise come first, because the spec says every such cell is `#CYCLE!`.\n- **Scale:** 99-row chains and `=SUM(A1:Z10)` work. So does a single chain through all 2,574 cells, which goes beyond what the spec asks.\n- **Speed:** a `set` now recalculates only the changed cell and the cells that depend on it, instead of the whole sheet. On a full sheet with a `get` after every `set`, that took the time from about 13.6 seconds to under 0.1 seconds.\n- **Odd input:** `=1e3` and `=1.2.3` give `#VALUE!`, `=0^0` gives 1, and `=\"5\"+1` gives 6.\n\nI checked this time that no code files had changed since my wave 2 commit, so there was no repeat of the replaced `sheet.mjs`."}
{"t":"2026-10-21T22:13:27.513Z","fault":"F4","what":"#CYCLE! renamed #CIRC!"}
{"t":"2026-10-21T22:13:49.058Z","event":"turn","n":5,"label":"wave 3 round 1","ok":true,"error":null,"context":92408,"cumulative":2250519,"cost":1.6599,"minutes":0.36,"said":"I've made the change: the cycle error is now `#CIRC!` instead of `#CYCLE!`. All 21 tests pass and it's committed.\n\nI renamed it in the error codes (`values.mjs`), where the sheet raises it (`sheet.mjs`), in my tests and in `ARCH.md`. How cycles are detected is unchanged; only the name of the error is different. `#CYCLE!` no longer appears anywhere in the code or tests."}
